  "result": "The gate returned **OK** on the first run, using 1 of the 6 allowed runs. It checked 6 witnesses and 7 names, and the rule composes no other rule.\n\nOne command was refused: a `grep` through the Core files, which this session isn't allowed to run. I read `Vocab/Primitives.lean` and part of `Vocab/Atoms.lean` with the Read tool instead, so nothing was lost.\n\n**The rule** (`LVMC_11_22_020.lean`):\n- **Who it covers:** the subject must be a member of the `DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle` group, written as one `ru_aggregate` atom.\n- **When it applies:** all three must hold:\n  - the subject occupies some highway region;\n  - `asm.within_city_limits` holds;\n  - the subject is moving faster than `p.halt_speed_tolerance`. This is how the node reads \"drive or operate\".\n- **What it requires** (an indirect test standing in for \"careless\"): no other road user, of any class, may either:\n  - touch the subject's body (`rel_contact`), or\n  - be on course to pass within `p.conflict_centre_clearance` of the subject within `p.conflict_horizon` (the closest-approach checks).\n\n  The subject itself is excluded from \"other road user\".\n- **No narrowings of my own:** the two narrowings the node records stay the plan's and are not repeated in the rule.\n\n**The witnesses:**\n- **The four planned scenarios:**\n  - `forbid`: the subject at 15 m/s heads for a halted car; they would pass 1 m apart in 2 s.\n  - `permit`: the subject is alone on the highway.\n  - `idle`: the subject is off the highway, and occupancy is observed, so \"not on a highway\" is decided rather than unknown.\n  - `blind`: occupancy is not observed and `rel.occupies` is masked, so the verdict is unknown.\n- **Two extra tests:**\n  - `branch_1`, violated: the bodies overlap while the other car pulls away, so contact alone decides it.\n  - `branch_2`, compliant: the cars are on course to pass 5 m apart, outside the 3 m clearance.\n\n`task_result.md` is written in the working directory.",
